; companion to pick-with-nested-quantifier.kurt: the alpha-equivalence fix to `equal_expr`
; must not become too permissive. A `pick` fact using a genuinely different predicate must
; still be rejected -- alpha-renaming leniency only applies to the bound-variable *names*
; themselves, never to any other symbol. (Not wrapped in `expect`: `pick` is itself a
; block-opening keyword, and expect's documented limitation -- it can't observe a failure
; from something that opens a further block of its own -- applies here too.)
load logic
bool R, Q
arity R 2
arity Q 2
use exists x (forall y (R x y))
pick c with forall y (Q c y)
    true
true
;;; ProofError: can not find an existential formula that matches the `pick`
